# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Golden Phat: Operational Security (.gitignore)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Principle: "Code in Git, Data on Disk."
# We explicitly ignore all scan results, evidence, and downloaded assets.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 1. Data Sovereignty (CRITICAL) ---
# Never commit findings, logs, or evidence to the repository.
pentest/runs/
pentest/evidence/
pentest/findings/
pentest/recon/
pentest/reports/
pentest/logs/
pentest/latest

# --- 2. Downloaded Assets ---
# Wordlists are large and should be fetched via 'make wordlists'
pentest/wordlists/

# --- 3. Local State & History ---
# Preserves operational security by not leaking command history
.container_bash_history
.python_history
.bash_history
.zsh_history

# --- 4. OS & Editor Noise ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- 5. Build Artifacts ---
# If you accidentally run 'go build' or 'cargo build' locally
vendor/
target/
bin/
go.sum
Cargo.lock
*.test
*.out

# --- 6. Explicit Whitelist ---
# We purposefully allow these to ensure the Scope is tracked.
# (Listed here for clarity, though not strictly required unless parents are ignored)
# !pentest/targets/scope.md
# !pentest/targets/targets.txt
